  "problem": {
    "statement": "JIRA Issue: DOC-3176\n\nTitle: Centralize Extension Logging Into OutputChannel\n\nDescription:\nReplace ad hoc console.log and console.error usage across the extension with a shared OutputChannel-backed logging utility, and migrate existing production logging to it.\n\nProblem:\nThe extension currently relies on console.log and console.error across activation, diagnostics, decorations, filesystem loading, and provider flows. These logs are only visible in developer tooling and are not accessible to normal extension users. This makes diagnosis harder, creates inconsistent log formatting, and does not align with standard VS Code extension logging practices.\n\nCurrent Evidence:\n- src/extension.ts\n- src/logic/lifecycle/pluginInit.ts\n- src/logic/lifecycle/pluginDispose.ts\n- src/logic/diagnostics/diagnosticHandlerWrapper.ts\n- src/logic/decorations/editorDecorations/editorDecorationTrigger.ts\n- src/logic/events/eventSubscriber.ts\n\nScope:\n- Create a shared logging module that owns a single vscode.window.createOutputChannel(...) instance.\n- Define lightweight log methods for info, warn, and error.\n- Replace existing console.log and console.error calls in production code under src/.\n- Ensure activation, deactivation, provider failures, debounce handlers, and background scanners log through the shared channel.\n- Keep tests free to stub logging without requiring DevTools console output.\n\nOut of Scope:\n- Telemetry backends or remote analytics.\n- Refactoring every subsystem into a new service architecture.\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\n- No console.log or console.error remain in production code under src/.\n- A dedicated Output channel exists and is named consistently.\n- Activation, deactivation, provider failures, and major background workflows log to the Output channel.\n- Log messages are concise, structured, and useful for debugging.\n- Existing behavior is preserved apart from where logs appear.\n- Full test suite for the new logging system.\n\nValidation:\n- Run the extension and confirm logs appear in the Output panel without opening DevTools.\n- Verify build, lint, and test suite still pass.\n- Confirm at least one activation log, one warning log, and one error log path are exercised in tests or manual verification.\n\nLabels: standards-alignment, vscode-refactor\n\nPriority: Normal\n\nWas this page helpful?: Helpful"
