      "message": {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Ralph Orchestrator Infrastructure Summary\n\nHere's the complete execution pipeline from Docker start to CLI execution to post-run hooks:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **Pipeline/Runner Scripts**\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/copilot-ralph-loop.sh`**\n- Loop driver for continuous Copilot CLI execution with configurable max iterations\n- Starts first turn with `copilot --prompt`, subsequent turns use `--continue`\n- Checks for completion promise marker in output\n- Manages iteration state in `.sisyphus/ralph-loop.json` (active, iteration count, max limits)\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/scripts/run-agent.ts`**\n- TypeScript entry point for local agent execution\n- Runs `AppStartup` to generate `.build/` files (MCP configs, overlays), starts containers (app + sidecar + proxy)\n- Executes Copilot CLI with prompt, collects logs to `output/logs/local-run-<timestamp>/`\n- Captures exit code and timeout flags via `ContainerExecResult` interface\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/scripts/run-hooks.ts`**\n- Replays post-task hooks from saved `hook-manifest.json`\n- Reads manifest from output directory, finds matching profile, builds DI cradle, executes hooks sequentially\n- Hooks are stored in manifest with execution context (artifact directories, target subagent names)\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Scientist/Run-Analyzer Agent Templates**\n\n**Ralph-Docs Profile:**\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/profiles/ralph-docs/agents/ralph.scientist.agent.md`**\n- **Description:** Post-task orchestrator — maps subagents, then dispatches per-subagent analysis and improvement\n- **Model:** Claude Opus 4.6 (non-user-invocable)\n- **Subagents:** `subagent-mapper`, `run-analyzer`, `agent-improver`, `run-synthesizer`\n- **Orchestration:** Reads cli-debug.log via mapper, extracts per-subagent spans/tools/tokens, fans out analyzer+improver per subagent\n- **Artifact root:** `{{ artifactDir }}/` (typically `.ralph/tasks/{{ taskId }}/artifacts/`)\n- **Status routing:** Reads `status.json` files, decides whether to dispatch improver based on analyzer result\n- **Output:** Writes final `scientist/status.json` with overall result (`improved`, `analyzed`, `skipped`, `error`)\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/profiles/ralph-docs/agents/ralph.run-analyzer.agent.md`**\n- **Description:** Post-task hook — analyzes completed agent execution logs (renders shared template)\n- **Model:** Claude Opus 4.6 (non-user-invocable)\n- **Input:** Mapper extraction file for a specific subagent (tool calls, tokens, errors, artifacts)\n- **Steps:** Tool analysis (selection quality, efficiency), token/context pressure, artifact quality (status.json completeness), error analysis, template variable resolution, gap identification\n- **Output path:** `{{ artifactDir }}/run-analyzer/<target-subagent-name>/output.md` and `status.json` (result: `analyzed`, `skipped`)\n- **Status codes:** Uses agent-eval skill for evaluation dimensions; distinguishes behavioral, rule, and infrastructure gaps\n\n**Ralph-Vscode Profile:**\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/profiles/ralph-vscode/agents/ralph.scientist.agent.md`**\n- **Description:** Simpler version — dispatches `run-analyzer` then `agent-improver` (not full fan-out like ralph-docs)\n- **Model:** Claude Opus 4.6 (non-user-invocable)\n- **Subagents:** `run-analyzer`, `agent-improver`\n- **Artifact root:** Same as ralph-docs\n- **Status routing:** Routes on analyzer result; if `analyzed`, dispatches improver; if `skipped` or `failed`, writes final status and exits\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/profiles/ralph-vscode/agents/ralph.scientist-run-analyzer.agent.md`**\n- **Description:** Alias/variant for run-analyzer (same template reference)\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Egress Proxy Configuration**\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/security/squid.conf`**\n- **Type:** Squid forward proxy domain allowlist configuration\n- **Listen port:** 3128\n- **Domain allowlist:** AI/LLM backends (`.githubcopilot.com`, `api.github.com`, `github.com`, `.anthropic.com`)\n- **Profile domains placeholder:** `{{PROFILE_DOMAINS}}` (auto-populated per profile)\n- **Host loopback access:** Allows `host.docker.internal:4500` (ralphchives RAG endpoint)\n- **Port rules:** Only HTTP (80) and HTTPS (443) allowed; CONNECT method only to port 443\n- **Caching:** Disabled; used as forward proxy only\n- **Logging:** Forwards to stdout via tail -F (on `/var/log/squid/access.log`)\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/security/docker-compose.security.yml`**\n- **Type:** Docker Compose security overlay (auto-merged with each profile's compose file)\n- **Services added:** `egress-proxy` (ubuntu/squid image)\n- **Network isolation:** Agent container on internal-only network (`ralph-internal`); Squid bridges to external network (`ralph-external`)\n- **Proxy env vars set in app:** `HTTP_PROXY`, `HTTPS_PROXY`, `http_proxy`, `https_proxy` → `http://egress-proxy:3128`\n- **NO_PROXY exemption:** `localhost,127.0.0.1,db,egress-proxy,mcp-sidecar`\n- **Security hardening:** `no-new-privileges:true`, capability drop (all), selective add (DAC_OVERRIDE, CHOWN)\n- **Resource limits:** 8GB memory limit, 4.0 CPU, 500 PIDs max; 2GB/1.0 CPU reserved\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Shared Includes — Error Handling & Pre-Flight**\n\n**Post-Hooks Directory:**\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/agent-includes/post-hooks/run-analyzer.md`**\n- **Full template** for run-analyzer agent (see section 2 for detailed content)\n- Defines evaluation dimensions, result codes, analysis procedures, gap identification methodology\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/agent-includes/post-hooks/run-synthesizer.md`**\n- Orchestrator-level + cross-subagent pattern synthesis after all per-subagent dispatches\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/agent-includes/post-hooks/agent-improver.md`**\n- Infrastructure improvement dispatch — modifies agent templates/skills/includes based on analyzer findings\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/agent-includes/post-hooks/subagent-mapper.md`**\n- Parses cli-debug.log, extracts per-subagent spans/tools/tokens/artifacts, writes structured inventory\n\n**Other Key Includes:**\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/agent-includes/agent-as-function-contract.md`**\n- Contract for status.json format (agent, task_id, status, result, summary, artifacts, next_hint, iteration)\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/agent-includes/prompt-security.md`**\n- Security guidance for handling sensitive prompt content in agent templates\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/agent-includes/personality/ralph.md`**\n- Ralph personality and behavior guidelines (included in ralph orchestrator)\n\n---\n\n### 5. **The Ralph Orchestrator**\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/profiles/ralph-docs/agents/ralph.ralph.agent.md`**\n- **Description:** Autonomous documentation orchestrator — routes researcher, writer, reviewers; commits and delivers doc tasks\n- **Model:** Claude Opus 4.6 (non-user-invocable)\n- **Primary subagents:** `ralph-researcher`, `ralph-planner`, `ralph-writer`, `ralph-reviewer-technical`, `ralph-reviewer-style`, `ralph-reviewer-ia`, `ralph-scribe`\n- **Optional:** `ralph-coder` (if `triggerParams.codesamples && triggerParams.xpversion`)\n- **Artifact root:** `.ralph/tasks/{{ taskId }}/artifacts/`\n- **Orchestration model:** Pure router — reads only `status.json` from subagents, decides routing based on result codes\n- **Strict ordering constraints:**\n  - Coder (if needed) BEFORE researcher\n  - Researcher BEFORE planner\n  - Planner BEFORE writer\n  - All reviewers BEFORE commit\n- **Review gate:** All three reviewers run; if any rejects, re-dispatch writer (max 3 revision rounds per task)\n- **What it does itself:** Commit (`git add`, `git commit`), Push (via `ado_push_progress` MCP), PR creation (via `ado_create_pull_request` MCP), JIRA greeting comment, exit block printing\n- **What it NEVER does:** Read subagent `output.md` (only `status.json`), relay content between subagents, research/write/review itself, compose/deliver handoff artifacts\n- **Exit block:** Prints `===RALPH_RESULT_START===` block with status (`completed`, `partial`, `blocked`, `error`)\n- **Revision support:** Includes alternative workflow if `isRevision: true` (previous feedback in prompt)\n\n---\n\n### 6. **Docker-Related Files**\n\n**Ralph-Docs Dockerfile:**\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/profiles/ralph-docs/Dockerfile`**\n- **Base:** Ubuntu 22.04 (multi-tool environment)\n- **Non-root user:** `vscode` (UID/GID 1000)\n- **Runtime stack:**\n  - Node.js 24 (from NodeSource)\n  - .NET SDK 10.0 (official install script)\n  - Ruby 3.3.8 (compiled from source to `/usr/local`)\n  - Pandoc 3.8.3 (for doc generation)\n  - SQL Server client tools (sqlcmd, msodbcsql18)\n  - Playwright + Chromium (headless browser testing)\n  - System deps: git, jq, ca-certificates, build essentials, locale setup (UTF-8)\n- **User-writable paths:** NPM prefix `/home/vscode/.npm-global`, Gem home `/home/vscode/.gems`\n- **Locale:** en_US.UTF-8 (required for Ruby UTF-8 file handling)\n\n**Ralph-Vscode Dockerfile:**\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/profiles/ralph-vscode/Dockerfile`**\n- **Base:** Node 22-bookworm-slim\n- **Non-root user:** Rename `node` to `vscode` (uid/gid 1000)\n- **Runtime:** Git, jq, ca-certificates, X11/Electron runtime libs (xvfb, xauth, libnss3, libnspr4, etc.)\n- **User-writable paths:** NPM prefix `/home/vscode/.npm-global`\n- **Purpose:** Lighter weight for Copilot CLI + VSCode extension development\n\n**Ralph-Docs docker-compose.yml:**\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/profiles/ralph-docs/docker-compose.yml`**\n- **Services:** `app` (main agent container), `db` (SQL Server 2022 for Xperience)\n- **Volume mounts:** `${TARGET_REPO_PATH}:/workspace` (target repo), `.ralph/` config/logs\n- **Environment:** `MSSQL_SA_PASSWORD`, `ADO_PAT_XPERIENCE`, `DB_HOST/PORT`\n- **Shared memory:** 2GB (`shm_size`)\n- **Networks:** `ralph-internal` (attached by security overlay)\n\n**Ralph-Vscode docker-compose.yml:**\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/profiles/ralph-vscode/docker-compose.yml`**\n- **Service:** `app` (single container)\n- **Volume:** `${TARGET_REPO_PATH}:/workspace`\n- **Shared memory:** 1GB\n- **Networks:** `ralph-internal` and `ralph-external` (for Squid sidecar)\n\n**MCP Sidecar Entrypoint:**\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/shared/mcp-sidecar/entrypoint.sh`**\n- **Function:** Runs MCP server pre-init scripts (if any), then launches gateway process manager\n- **Pre-init script:** `/opt/mcp/pre-init.sh` (auto-generated from MCP server initScript declarations)\n- **Gateway:** Hands off to Node.js gateway at `/opt/mcp/gateway/dist/gateway.js` with config `/opt/mcp/config/gateway.json`\n- **Error handling:** Non-fatal pre-init failures continue (logs warning)\n\n---\n\n### 7. **CLI Execution & Stdout/Stderr Capture**\n\n**Copilot Executor: `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/src/container/cli-executors/copilot-executor.ts`**\n- **CLI paths:**\n  - Config dir: `/workspace/.ralph`\n  - Debug log dir: `/workspace/.ralph/logs/cli-debug`\n  - Transcript: `/workspace/.ralph/logs/session-transcript.md`\n  - Prompt file: `/workspace/.ralph/prompt.txt` (avoids shell escaping issues)\n  - Writable dirs: `.ralph/logs`, `.ralph/logs/cli-debug`, `.ralph/session-state`\n- **Execution method:** `docker compose exec --user vscode app sh -c \"<copilot command>\"`\n- **Command structure:**\n  ```bash\n  exec copilot \\\n    --config-dir /workspace/.ralph \\\n    --additional-mcp-config @/workspace/.ralph/mcp-config.json \\\n    --agent <agentName> \\\n    --model <model> \\\n    --log-level debug \\\n    --log-dir /workspace/.ralph/logs/cli-debug \\\n    --experimental --allow-all-tools --allow-all-paths \\\n    --share /workspace/.ralph/logs/session-transcript.md \\\n    -p \"$(cat /workspace/.ralph/prompt.txt)\"\n  ```\n- **Continuation:** Uses `--continue --prompt` for resuming sessions\n- **Stream capture:** Real-time stdout/stderr streaming to container logger via `executeCliCommand`\n- **Exit code capture:** Returns `ContainerExecResult` with `exitCode`, `stdout`, `stderr`, `timedOut` flag\n\n**Result Parser: `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/src/container/result-parser.ts`**\n- **Result block format:** `===RALPH_RESULT_START===...===RALPH_RESULT_END===`\n- **Extracts from block:** `PR_URL` and `STATUS` (case-insensitive)\n- **Status priority:** Agent-reported status > timeout > exit code\n- **Valid status codes:** `completed`, `partial`, `blocked`, `error`\n- **Fallback:** Loose regex for PR URL if structured block missing\n- **Exit code mapping:**\n  - 0 → `completed`\n  - Non-zero → `error` (or `partial` if timed out)\n  - Agent status takes precedence (e.g., agent can return `partial` even if exit 0)\n\n**Continuation Runner: `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/src/container/continuation-runner.ts`**\n- **Retry loop:** If session ends without `===RALPH_RESULT_START===`, re-invokes with `--continue` and exponential backoff\n- **Continuation prompt:** Notifies agent that previous session incomplete, asks to output result block\n- **Max attempts:** Configurable (default ~5 attempts)\n- **Exit condition:** Result block found or max attempts exhausted\n\n---\n\n### 8. **Post-Run Hooks & Manifest**\n\n**Hook Manifest: `/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/src/services/task-runner.ts`**\n- **File location:** `<outputDir>/hook-manifest.json`\n- **Contents:**\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"taskId\": \"string\",\n    \"workItemId\": \"string\",\n    \"source\": \"string\",\n    \"profileId\": \"string\",\n    \"variantKey\": \"string\",\n    \"triggerParams\": { \"key\": \"string\" },\n    \"isRevision\": boolean,\n    \"outputDir\": \"string\",\n    \"status\": \"string\",\n    \"collectedLogs\": { \"id\": \"path\" },\n    \"hooks\": [{ \"name\", \"displayName\", \"template\", ... }],\n    \"createdAt\": \"ISO-8601 timestamp\"\n  }\n  ```\n- **Purpose:** Enables replay of post-task hooks without re-running primary agent\n- **Hook execution:** `run-hooks.ts` reads manifest, finds profile, builds DI cradle, executes hooks sequentially\n\n**Log Collection:**\n\n**`/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/src/container/log-collector.ts`**\n- **Sources captured per execution:**\n  - `audit` (jsonl) — from `profile.auditLogPath`\n  - `transcript` (md) — from `CopilotExecutor.TRANSCRIPT_PATH`\n  - `proxy` (log) — from `/var/log/squid/access.log`\n  - `sidecar` (log) — from MCP sidecar container\n  - `cli-debug` — from Copilot's debug log directory\n- **Modes:** `Collect` (copy to output), `Stream` (tail -F in real-time)\n- **Output location:** `output/logs/<taskId-timestamp>/` with prefixed filenames per source\n\n---\n\n### 9. **Exit Block Contract**\n\nAgents must output (typically at task completion):\n```\n===RALPH_RESULT_START===\nPR_URL: <url or \"none\">\nSTATUS: completed|partial|blocked|error\n===RALPH_RESULT_END===\n```\n\n**Interpretation:**\n- `completed` — task fully done, PR ready\n- `partial` — some work done, some gaps/failures, PR ready\n- `blocked` — cannot proceed, waiting for external action or information\n- `error` — fatal failure, no valid output produced\n\n---\n\n### 10. **Full Execution Flow Summary**\n\n1. **Startup (`AppStartup`):** Validates config, builds MCP servers, generates `.build/` files (configs, overlays)\n2. **Container launch:** Starts app + sidecar + proxy containers with security overlay, binds target repo to `/workspace`\n3. **CLI execution:** Copilot CLI runs inside container with agent name, model, MCP config, debug logs enabled\n4. **Prompt injection:** Large prompts written to file to avoid shell escaping; MCP tools rendered into prompt\n5. **Stream capture:** stdout/stderr captured in real-time to container logger\n6. **Result parsing:** After CLI finishes, extract PR URL and status from `===RALPH_RESULT_START===` block\n7. **Exit code resolution:** Determine final `TaskStatus` (completed/partial/blocked/error) from agent status, exit code, timeout flag\n8. **Continuation (if needed):** If result block missing, retry with `--continue` up to max attempts\n9. **Log collection:** Gather audit, transcript, proxy, sidecar logs to `output/logs/<taskId>/`\n10. **Hook manifest:** Write `hook-manifest.json` with all context for later hook replay\n11. **Post-task hooks:** If configured, dispatch scientist agent (or custom hooks) to analyze execution and suggest improvements\n12. **Hook replay:** Later, `run-hooks.ts` can replay hooks without re-running primary agent\n\n---\n\n**Key File Locations Summary:**\n\n| Component | File |\n|-----------|------|\n| CLI launcher | `scripts/run-agent.ts`, `copilot-ralph-loop.sh` |\n| Hook replayer | `scripts/run-hooks.ts` |\n| Copilot executor | `src/container/cli-executors/copilot-executor.ts` |\n| Result parser | `src/container/result-parser.ts` |\n| Continuation runner | `src/container/continuation-runner.ts` |\n| Log collector | `src/container/log-collector.ts` |\n| Task runner (manifest writer) | `src/services/task-runner.ts` |\n| Scientist template (ralph-docs) | `profiles/ralph-docs/agents/ralph.scientist.agent.md` |\n| Run-analyzer template | `shared/agent-includes/post-hooks/run-analyzer.md` |\n| Ralph orchestrator | `profiles/ralph-docs/agents/ralph.ralph.agent.md` |\n| Squid proxy config | `shared/security/squid.conf` |\n| Security overlay | `shared/security/docker-compose.security.yml` |\n| Ralph-docs Dockerfile | `profiles/ralph-docs/Dockerfile` |\n| Ralph-vscode Dockerfile | `profiles/ralph-vscode/Dockerfile` |\n| MCP sidecar entrypoint | `shared/mcp-sidecar/entrypoint.sh` |",
